# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the contrib leak gate.
#
# Suppression is by MODULE, which is the whole reason this gate uses LSan
# rather than valgrind: the CI driver is lavapipe, and valgrind cannot follow
# its LLVM JIT (one render reports ~13k errors from ~1000 contexts, all inside
# the loader or the driver's worker threads). LSan matches these patterns
# against the module each frame resolves to, so allocations owned by the
# graphics stack are excluded by object while every allocation this repo makes
# is still gated.
#
# Keep this list minimal and module-shaped. A pattern naming a function in our
# own code would hide a real leak.

# Mesa's software Vulkan driver (lavapipe). Keeps one allocation per process
# alive past exit: its instance dispatch is torn down after the last
# vkDestroyInstance returns.
leak:libvulkan_lvp

# The Vulkan loader itself, and the ICDs it may load on a machine with real
# hardware (the gate must behave the same on a developer box).
leak:libvulkan.so
leak:libvulkan_radeon
leak:libvulkan_intel
leak:libvulkan_virtio

# LLVM, which lavapipe JITs through.
leak:libLLVM

# The GL/DRM stack the drivers pull in.
leak:libdrm
leak:libgallium
leak:libglapi
